XR64 - R64_UINT over the no-list 64-bit class, with and without UBWC (exp-23)
Date of runs: 2026-11-21. Curated; raw logs: results/raw/xr64-p14.log,
results/raw/xr64-exp23-knoboff.log, results/raw/xr64-exp23-knobon.log.

QUESTION (open question 14 in docs/plan-next-checks.md)
    The 64-bit compatibility class is the last class whose UBWC was never asked,
    and its member R64_UINT has no texture and no colour path, so the only
    reader it has is a storage image. A list that NAMES R64_UINT can never be
    compressed (fd6_ubwc_compat_mode() answers FD6_UBWC_UNKNOWN_COMPAT and a list
    with an UNKNOWN member is refused before labels are compared), so the only
    create where an R64_UINT view is legal AND the image could be compressed is
    one made without a list. Probe XR64 asks it: fill by buffer->image copy in
    the base format, read every 64-bit word through a r64ui storage image, then
    imageAtomicAdd(+1) per word and read again.

