FEATURES THE PROBE NEEDS (printed by the test before the device is created)
    xr64 features: shaderInt64=1, shaderImageInt64Atomics=1,
                   sparseImageInt64Atomics=0
    - the two it uses are there (props.has_64b_image_atomics); the third is not,
      so a sparse image with 64-bit atomics is not covered by any run here.

HOW TO READ THE XR64/XMC ROWS (they are easy to misread later)
    "N/M wrong" counts disagreement with the EXPECTED pattern; "N would be the
    swapped halves" / "would be the reversed word" counts disagreement with the
    ALTERNATIVE pattern, so a row that says `0/262144 wrong, 262144 would be the
    swapped halves` is a clean read, not a problem. tail=0x2000 means a UBWC
    metadata plane is allocated; that is the layout claim, not proof that the
    compressor ran (journal 22.2) - on a740 no counter can show that
    (UCHE_GMEM_* read 0, the UBWC counters do not fit the UCHE budget of 12).

